    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1518">

                <pb facs="1201" n="1191" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1191"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.8576/6–3049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-30T17:00:00+08:00">June 30, 1949—5 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 30—9:42 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2570. Reliable source states that Chen Yi has recommended tongs being against
                    plan to rush Consulate reported in mytel 2466, June 24, repeated Nanking 1331,
                    and 2536 June 29, repeated Nanking 1382.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 2570, repeated Nanking 1409.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
